          <p>A true composited workspace: compared, annotated, rearranged live. A panel composites on its own glass. Polaris composites and then encodes the whole canvas back out, both to remote participants who never joined a call and to a browser on any device. That is meeting parity: everyone in the room and everyone remote is looking at the same content at the same time, with no second-class view. That is the line the panel vendors have not crossed.</p>
